      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "Më pëlqen …",
      "text": "\"Më pëlqen buka\" works the other way round from English: \"the bread pleases me\". Më means \"to me\", pëlqen means \"pleases\", and the thing you like comes last with its \"the\" ending: buka, kafeja, uji. For \"you like\" say të pëlqen.",
